Package: mzLibR
Title: R Bindings for the mzLib Proteomics Library
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("trishorts", email = "mshort@chem.wisc.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Calls the mzLib proteomics library from R over a language-neutral
    bridge: PRIDE repository access, in-silico digestion and fragmentation of
    peptidoforms, and label-free quantification with match-between-runs via
    FlashLFQ. The bridge is a self-contained executable that carries its own
    .NET runtime, so no .NET installation is required. It is shared with the
    Python ('pyMzLib') and Rust ('mzLibRust') bindings, which means all three
    agree field for field.
License: LGPL (>= 3)
URL: https://github.com/smith-chem-wisc/mzLibR
BugReports: https://github.com/smith-chem-wisc/mzLibR/issues
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0)
Imports: utils
Encoding: UTF-8
NeedsCompilation: no
